{%- comment -%}
  One quarter of a 2x2 mashup.

  Below lg that quarter is about 375x215 — room for a single sensor, so it
  shows the first entry in the priority list. On TRMNL X the same quarter is
  about 500x345, which is two of the full screen's cards side by side, and
  one big number there left most of the quarter empty.
{%- endcomment -%}

{%- if fault != '' -%}
  {% render 'notice', headline: 'Ruuvi', detail: fault %}
{%- else -%}
  <div class="layout layout--col layout--center lg:hidden{% if primary.is_stale %} text--gray-30{% endif %}">
    <div class="flex flex--row gap--xsmall">
      <span class="label" data-clamp="1">{{ primary.name }}</span>
      {% render 'sensor_flags', sensor: primary %}
    </div>

    {%- if primary.status == 'no_data' -%}
      <span class="value value--large">&mdash;</span>
      <span class="label label--small">no data</span>
    {%- else -%}
      <span class="value value--xlarge value--tnums">{{ primary.temperature }}&deg;C</span>
      <div class="flex flex--row gap--medium">
        <span class="value value--small value--tnums">{{ primary.humidity | default: '&mdash;' }}%</span>
        <span class="value value--small value--tnums">{{ primary.pressure_hpa | default: '&mdash;' }} hPa</span>
      </div>
      <span class="label label--small">{{ primary.measured_at }}</span>
    {%- endif -%}
  </div>

  {%- comment -%}
    Two sensors, in priority order. A portrait X turns the quarter on its
    side — 375x475 — where two columns would leave each card about 180px,
    too narrow for the hero once text_scale has its share. One column of two
    cards is what that shape holds, so `wide` applies here as well.
  {%- endcomment -%}
  <div class="layout layout--col hidden lg:flex ruuvi">
    <div class="grid grid--cols-2 portrait:grid--cols-1 gap--small ruuvi__grid">
      {%- for sensor in featured limit: 2 -%}
        {%- assign rank_label = forloop.index | prepend: '0' -%}
        {% render 'sensor_card', sensor: sensor, rank: forloop.index, rank_label: rank_label, wide: true %}
      {%- endfor -%}
    </div>
  </div>
{%- endif -%}

<div class="title_bar">
  <span class="title">Ruuvi</span>
</div>
